      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-66062: scaling the cosecant range by 5 and subtracting 3 gives values at most -8 or at least 2. q-66074: secant is undefined when 3x-60°=90°+180°n, giving x=50°+60°n. For the quadratic inequalities, the roots and opening directions give: q-75976 [-2,4]; q-24351 the exterior intervals including -2 and 3; q-144414 (-2,0); q-141187 the exterior intervals excluding -5 and -1; q-115287 (-7,1); q-31015 (2,4). q-23799: tan(theta)(1-sin²(theta))=sin(theta)cos(theta), so the quotient is 1/2 wherever the original expression is defined. q-65231: factoring cos²(x)=(1-sin(x))(1+sin(x)) gives f(x)=1+sin(x) on the original domain. q-31585: two applications of L'Hopital's rule give -e⁰/cos(0)=-1. q-115530: two applications give the limit of sqrt(x)/8, which is positive infinity. q-2403: differentiating (ln(x))^(1/2)/(2x) gives (1-2ln(x))/(4x²sqrt(ln(x))) for x>1. Matrix subscripts specify row then column, giving q-125561=-3, q-13497=5, and q-125593=1. The source's references to blue markings differ from the orange interval markings shown, and q-125593 labels its displayed matrix E instead of R; these incidental source errors do not change the answers. No prior submitted answers or grades were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
